The forward direction is immediate from Equation . Acting in one order gives $\begin{aligned}
ML\ket{i}
&=M\bigl(l_i\ket{i}\bigr)\\
&=l_i m_i\ket{i},\end{aligned}$ while the reverse order gives $\begin{aligned}
LM\ket{i}
&=L\bigl(m_i\ket{i}\bigr)\\
&=m_i l_i\ket{i}.\end{aligned}$ The eigenvalues are ordinary numbers, so $l_i m_i=m_i l_i$. Thus $ML$ and $LM$ act identically on every member of a basis and hence on every state: $\equiv LM-ML=0.$

