The standard phrase expectation value means a statistical average. For an observable $L$, $\expect{L}(t)=\bra{\psi(t)}L\ket{\psi(t)}.$ Only the state vectors carry time dependence at this stage. Differentiating both sides and using Equation  together with its Hermitian conjugate, $\frac{d}{dt}\ket{\psi}=-iH\ket{\psi},
\qquad
\frac{d}{dt}\bra{\psi}=i\bra{\psi}H,$ gives $\begin{aligned}
\frac{d}{dt}\expect{L}
&=i\bra{\psi}HL\ket{\psi}
  -i\bra{\psi}LH\ket{\psi}\\
&=-i\expect{[L,H]}.
\end{aligned}$

