The expectation value of $L$ can now be written explicitly. Define its matrix elements in the energy basis by $L_{kj}=\bra{E_k}L\ket{E_j}.$ Then $\begin{aligned}
\expect{L}(t)
&=\sum_{k,j}
\alpha_k^*(0)\alpha_j(0)
e^{i(E_k-E_j)t}
L_{kj}.
\end{aligned}$

